  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">Increased kinetic strikes that damage or disable oilfields, pumping stations, pipelines and export infrastructure force producers to shut wells and processing trains, directly lowering utilization of installed crude production capacity.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">energy_supply_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::kinetic_strike_intensity" target="energy_supply_shock::refined_inventory_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained attacks on refineries, storage depots and fuel transport routes disrupt refining throughput and deliveries, causing regional on‑hand refined fuel stocks to be drawn down as supply is interrupted and logistical buffers are consumed.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">energy_supply_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::kinetic_strike_intensity" target="global_bond_turmoil::bond_market_volatility" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Periods of elevated battlefield strikes materially raise near‑term geopolitical and commodity‑supply uncertainty, triggering rapid repricing and larger intraday swings in sovereign and corporate bond prices and yields.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_bond_turmoil</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::kinetic_strike_intensity" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::compute_resource_conc" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Destructive strikes on Ukrainian data centers, fiber routes and local hosting capacity force commercial and research workloads to be migrated quickly to large, geographically safer cloud providers, concentrating high-performance compute capacity with a smaller set of hyperscalers.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
