<edge source="us_iran_confrontation::maritime_incident_rate" target="energy_supply_shock::energy_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">A rising frequency of naval confrontations in key chokepoints raises shipping risk premiums, insurance and freight costs and generates an immediate market risk premium that pushes up spot energy prices.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_confrontation</data>
  <data key="d40">energy_supply_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_confrontation::maritime_incident_rate" target="global_bond_turmoil::bond_market_volatility" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">A spike in naval confrontations at choke points produces episodic shipping/insurance shocks and sudden portfolio re‑hedging (duration rebalances and liquidity withdrawals) that produce larger intraday and interday swings in global sovereign bond prices and yields.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_confrontation</data>
  <data key="d40">global_bond_turmoil</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_confrontation::maritime_incident_rate" target="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_pressure_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A rise in attacks/interdictions on commercial shipping and chokepoints increases energy security and insurance shocks that make governments reluctant to expand or strictly enforce additional sanctions on Russian energy for fear of exacerbating supply disruptions.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_confrontation</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_confrontation::maritime_incident_rate" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::industrial_policy_streng" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">An uptick in naval confrontations around key chokepoints spurs governments to subsidize domestic manufacturing, secure ports, and onshore critical technology production (including AI hardware and sovereign data centers) as protective industrial policy measures.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_confrontation</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
