<edge source="us_iran_confrontation::oil_flow_disruption_rate" target="energy_supply_shock::energy_supply_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">Direct physical interruptions to tankers, terminals, pipelines or chokepoints (attacks, seizures, closure) immediately reduce the volumetric deliveries of crude and refined products to markets.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_confrontation</data>
  <data key="d40">energy_supply_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_confrontation::oil_flow_disruption_rate" target="global_bond_turmoil::long_term_bond_yield" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Direct interruptions to crude and refined product shipments raise near‑term energy prices and add a persistent geopolitical term premium on sovereign debt (through growth/inflation risk and sovereign risk reassessment), lifting long‑duration yields.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_confrontation</data>
  <data key="d40">global_bond_turmoil</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_confrontation::oil_flow_disruption_rate" target="russia_ukraine_war::dipl_engagement_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Repeated disruptions to crude and product flows prompt urgent multilateral and bilateral diplomacy (emergency energy talks, sanction carve‑out negotiations, transit diplomacy) that raises the tempo of diplomatic activity touching the Russia–Ukraine conflict arena.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_confrontation</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_confrontation::oil_flow_disruption_rate" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::compute_resource_conc" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Repeated interruptions to oil shipments raise energy price volatility and logistical risk for shipping server hardware and fuel for data centers, pushing firms to consolidate workloads with a few hyperscalers and cloud providers that can secure long‑term power and logistics contracts, increasing compute concentration.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_confrontation</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
