  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Episodes of acute bond-market volatility raise political and policymaker risk aversion, prompting faster or tougher regulatory interventions (capital controls, export controls, tighter oversight) aimed at shielding strategic tech sectors during financial stress.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_turmoil</data>
