<edge source="energy_supply_shock::energy_supply_flow" target="global_bond_turmoil::bond_market_volatility" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">An abrupt drop in energy supply flows triggers sharp repricing in commodity and derivatives markets that forces deleveraging and margin calls in intermediary balance sheets, spilling over into fixed‑income liquidity and causing larger and more frequent bond price and yield swings.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_supply_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">global_bond_turmoil</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_supply_shock::energy_supply_flow" target="russia_ukraine_war::kinetic_strike_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">A rapid decline in delivered fuel volumes to the conflict theater reduces available fuel for armored, ground and air platforms, constraining operational tempos and lowering the frequency and scale of kinetic strikes.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_supply_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_supply_shock::energy_supply_flow" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::industrial_policy_streng" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">A measurable reduction in energy flows exposes supply vulnerabilities, prompting governments to strengthen industrial policy (subsidies, local content rules, strategic investment) to insulate critical technology and manufacturing sectors from energy shocks.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_supply_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
