<edge source="energy_supply_shock::sanction_intensity" target="global_bond_turmoil::cross_border_flows" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">An increase in energy‑related sanctions and trade restrictions directly interrupts payment channels, freezes or seizes assets and forces banks and funds to halt or redirect transactions, thereby reducing and rerouting net cross‑border capital and trade flows.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_supply_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">global_bond_turmoil</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_supply_shock::sanction_intensity" target="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Sharper, more far‑reaching energy-related sanctions impose asymmetric burdens on alliance members, provoking disputes over exemptions and burden-sharing that erode political and policy alignment.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_supply_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_supply_shock::sanction_intensity" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::geopolitical_tension" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">An uptick in energy‑related sanctions and trade restrictions directly escalates interstate disputes and reciprocal measures, hardening diplomatic stances and raising strategic tensions between the US and China.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_supply_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_supply_shock::sanction_intensity" target="us_iran_confrontation::retaliation_momentum" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Rapid escalation in energy-related sanctions constrains Iran's economic outlets and signals coercion, prompting Iranian leadership to authorize or accelerate asymmetric retaliatory attacks and proxy operations that feed a tit‑for‑tat escalation dynamic.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_supply_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_confrontation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_supply_shock::sanction_intensity" target="us_iran_confrontation::maritime_incident_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Broader, stricter sanctions force Iran and allied actors to rely on opaque shipping practices and convoying tactics that increase interceptions, boarding attempts and confrontations with naval forces, raising the frequency of maritime incidents.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_supply_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_confrontation</data>
</edge>
