  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">A sustained rise in energy prices directly lifts headline consumer prices and input costs for transport and production, prompting households and markets to revise up near‑term and medium‑term inflation expectations.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_supply_shock</data>
