  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained higher energy prices raise domestic economic and political costs for energy‑dependent sanctioning states, reducing their willingness to maintain or escalate broad, tightly enforced sanctions measures.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_supply_shock</data>
